The HW-NAS proved capable of producing a tiny CNN that needs 4.9 times less RAM and 12.7 times less Flash than the one adopted in \cite{chen2020improved}. Notably, such CNN scored higher test accuracy while decreasing latency. The resulting architecture can run on an STM32-L010RBT6, i.e., an ultra-low-power MCU, and is therefore suitable for IIoT sensor nodes. 

