\subsection{Results comparing classification with regression}
\label{subsec:CvsR}

Figure \ref{fig:classification_vs_regression} compares the total time required to build the CADs in our test dataset using the variable ordering suggested by each model.  We see that the KNN, and SVM, models all perform better under the regression paradigm, while the RF, MLP, and XGBoost models perform worse.  Overall, the best performance on the dataset is achieved by a model under the regression paradigm.  So the results partially validate our hypothesis that regression can use extra information to improve performance on the choice, but with the substantial caveat that it is model dependent.

