\begin{abstract}
Accurate channel state information (CSI) acquisition for massive multiple-input multiple-output (MIMO) systems is essential for future mobile communication networks. Channel fingerprint (CF), also referred to as channel knowledge map, is a key enabler for intelligent environment-aware communication and can facilitate CSI acquisition. However, due to the cost limitations of practical sensing nodes and test vehicles, the resulting CF is typically coarse-grained, making it insufficient for wireless transceiver design. In this work, we introduce the concept of CF twins and design a \textit{conditional} generative diffusion model (CGDM) with strong implicit prior learning capabilities as the computational core of the CF twin to establish the connection between coarse- and fine-grained CFs. Specifically, we employ a variational inference technique to derive the evidence lower bound (ELBO) for the log-marginal distribution of the observed fine-grained CF \textit{conditioned} on the coarse-grained CF, enabling the CGDM to learn the complicated distribution of the target data. During the denoising neural network optimization, the coarse-grained CF is introduced as \textit{side information} to accurately guide the conditioned generation of the CGDM. To make the proposed CGDM lightweight, we further leverage the additivity of network layers and introduce a one-shot pruning approach along with a multi-objective knowledge distillation technique. Experimental results show that the proposed approach exhibits significant improvement in reconstruction performance compared to the baselines. Additionally, zero-shot testing on reconstruction tasks with different magnification factors further demonstrates the scalability and generalization ability of the proposed approach.

%Experimental results show that, for the fine-grained CF reconstruction task with a $\times4$ magnification factor, the proposed model achieves significant performance gains over the baselines. Additionally, to further evaluate the scalability and generalization ability of the proposed model, we conducted zero-shot testing on fine-grained CF reconstruction tasks with magnification factors of $\times2$, $\times8$, and $\times16$, and performed a comprehensive comparison with the baselines.



%去实现6G移动通信网络的宏大目标需要准确的获取信道状态信息for大维甚至超大维度无线信道在MIMO系统中。为此，人们可以利用显著增强的传感能力和AI计算能力来推动environment-unaware communication到智能的环境感知通信的范式转变。信道指纹，也称之为信道知识库或信道知识地图，作为环境感知通信的关键使能者，可以有效facilitate channel state information (CSI) acquisition.然而，受到实际感知节点和测试车在成本上的限制，导致所得到的CF几乎是粗颗粒度的，其不能准确的指导无线传输设计。为此，我们提出了信道指纹孪生的概念，将物理传播环境和粗颗粒的CF作为物理对象，并将细颗粒的CF作为虚拟孪生对象。为了建立二者之间的联系，我们引入了当下具备强有力隐式先验分布学习能力的GDM作为信道指纹孪生的计算中枢。具体地，we apply a variational inference technique to derive the evidence lower bound (ELBO) of the objective， allows the GDM to learn the true distribution of the target data。此外，during the denoising network optimization，我们引入了the coarse-grained CF serves as side information去引导GDM的有方向性的生成细颗粒度CF. 为了进一步轻量化上述所提出的CGDM，我们基于网络层之间的可加性质，提出一种一次性剪枝方法和知识蒸馏技术。实验结果表明在*4的细颗粒CF重构任务上，所提出的模型相较于基线们有着明显的性能增益。此外，为了验证所提出模型的可扩展和泛化能力，我们也在*2，*16，*8的细颗粒CF重构任务上进行了zero-shot测试，进一步验证了我们模型具备很好的知识迁移能力。














\end{abstract}

