\subsection{Evaluation Protocol}

The evaluation protocol mirrored that of the VLM experiments to ensure a consistent comparison. The validation set consisted of the full 15,000 synthetic images. Due to the CRNN model's high inference speed, we evaluated it on the entire set, in contrast to the 1,000-sample subset used for reporting VLM performance. The real-world test set was identical, containing 218 handwritten Manchu words. All metrics (word accuracy, character error rate (CER), and F1 score) were computed using the same implementations as in the VLM assessment.

