\begin{lemma}\label{lemma:mdollar}
Let ${\cal M} = (T_1,T_2,\ldots,T_m)$ be a string collection. Then 

\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mdollar({\cal M}) \same \mdollarE({\cal M})$. Moreover, \$$_d$ in $\mdollarE({\cal M})$ is replaced by \$$_{d-1}$ in $\mdollar({\cal M})$, and \$$_1$ by \$$_m$. 
%
