\section{Introduction}

Inspired by natural organisms, many shape-changing robots have been proposed. Utilizing soft materials, soft robotic grippers perform tasks where traditional rigid grippers suffer such as adaptive manipulation and safe handling of delicate objects \cite{wang2017prestressed}. Soft grasping can be categorized into three approaches \cite{shintake2018soft}: actuation, controlled stiffness and controlled adhesion. Actuation and controlled adhesion methods typically involve control systems for motors or soft materials \cite{wang2023self}. Recently, research in soft grasping has shifted toward performing grasping tasks while minimizing control complexity \cite{gilday2020suction}. 

