\subsection{Working Stages} 

% The self-closing mechanism is two folds. First, the deformation of the cup, the middle part move upward, the two edges move downward, forming a 'n' shape concave, two edges closes within the deformation upon contact with the objects. Second is the adhesion of the disk when working on a powerful vacuum blower. Based on the Bernouli's law, the high air flow will lead to a relatively small air pressure, and a force will be produced to push the disk to adhesere to the object. This is fully passive process.


The operation of the hybrid gripper involves three stages. \textcolor{black}{The granules first flow upon contact with the object, enabling the gripper to conform to its contours.} As the gripper continues to approach, the granules are compressed against the base. Activating the vacuum then induces a stiffness transition in the granules from a flexible to a rigid state. For small objects, the porous interface may cause insufficient airtight seal \textcolor{black}{that results in consistent airflow and pressure on the sealing lip.} In the last stage, vacuum flow is regulated, enhancing adhesion and airtightness to ensure a secure grasp.










