\begin{restatable}{theorem}{MLHThard}\label{thm:MTLT-NPhard}
The MLHT problem is NP-hard in $\Reals^2$.
\end{restatable}
\begin{proof}
    We use a reduction from the Euclidean Steiner Tree problem. Let $P$ be a set of $n$ points in $\Reals^2$. Choose any point $p^* \in P$ and let $\Delta$ be obtained by translating $P$ such that $p^*$ is at the origin, that is, $\Delta = \{p - p^*\mid p \in P\setminus\{p^*\}\}$. We now show that there exists an EST $Y$ on $P$ of length at most $L$ if and only if the MLHT of $\Delta$ has length at most $L$. 

