\subsection{Multi-Band Sensing with RAREs}
% The granularity of wireless sensing is continuously refined by increasing the signal frequency.
% This is due to the fact that a minor disturbance in the signal transmission delay, $d$, caused by the displacement of target can lead to a sharp change in the signal phase, $\frac{\omega d}{c}$, when the frequency $\omega$ is large. 
