Our experiments indicate that such redundant executions account for approximately 90\% of the behavioral node simulation time. %in the RTL fault simulation. 
Consequently, the key to improving fault simulation performance is to eliminate these redundant executions. 
Existing RTL fault simulation frameworks \cite{mozart, multi_cs} detect the inputs to each node, and for a behavioral node, if its faulty inputs match the good inputs, the corresponding fault simulation is skipped.

