\subsection{Implicit Redundancy Elimination and Fault Simulation on Behavioral Nodes}\label{behavioral}

To efficiently eliminate redundant execution in behavioral nodes, we propose Algorithm~\ref{alg_execution}, an execution flow redundancy elimination approach. Algorithm~\ref{alg_execution} takes behavior nodes, and fault id as input. 
By using the good execution path as a reference and monitoring the path decision nodes and path dependency nodes, it detects the redundant execution of faulty behavioral codes where the fault input differs from the good input but the output remains consistent with the good behavioral codes.
% To achieve the aforementioned goal, Algorithm~\ref{alg_execution} consists of four main steps: preprocessing of RTL code blocks, visibility dependency graph construction for input signal, path decision nodes evaluation, and path dependency nodes evaluation. 
We describe the Algorithm~\ref{alg_execution} in the context of a circuit case, as shown in Fig.~\ref{elimination}.
% Next, we illustrate how Algorithm~\ref{alg_execution} operates on RTL code blocks using the example shown in Fig.~\ref{elimination}.

% 为实现上述目标，算法1的主要包括3个步骤：RTL代码块的预处理，路径决策点判断和路径依赖点判断。下面，我们结合图5的举例，来展示算法1如何在RTL代码块上工作。

\begin{algorithm}
% \caption{Execution Flow Redundancy Elimination} 
\caption{Implicit Redundancy Elimination} 
\label{alg_execution}
\KwIn{ Behavior\_code: A fault-free behavioral code; fault\_id: Specified the faulty behavioral code}
\KwOut{The faulty behavioral code is redundant or not }
CFG $\gets$ build\_control\_flow\_graph(Behavior\_code)\;
VDG $\gets$ build\_visibility\_dependency\_graph(CFG)\;
cur $\gets$ the entry node of VDG\; 
% \If{! has\_RTL\_events(Behavioral\_code, fault\_id)}{
% \Return true\;
% }
% \tcp{Redundancy Identification}
\While{ cur not null} { 
    \If{cur is path decision node}{
        next\_good\_node $\gets$ Evaluate(good gates)\;
        next\_fault\_node $\gets$ Evaluate(bad gates)\;
        \If{ next\_good\_node $\neq$ next\_fault\_node}{
            \Return false\;
        }
    } 
    \If {cur is path dependency node}{
        \ForEach{signal $\in$ cur} {
            \If{IsVisible(signal, fault\_id)} {
                \Return false\;
            }
        }
    }
    cur $\gets$ next\_node;
}
% \tcp{\textcolor{blue}{For Synchronization}}
% add\_write\_permission(Behavior\_code, fault\_id)\; 
\Return true\;
\end{algorithm} 

