\subsection{Explicit execution redundancy detection}\label{behavioral_explicit}


% To achieve the RTL fault simulation, it is essential to conduct fault simulation on the RTL nodes. Due to the arbitrary bit width of logic values in the RTL graph, traditional fault simulation techniques that leverage parallel processing of machine words, such as parallel fault and parallel pattern fault simulation, are unfeasible.
% Therefore, we extend the concurrent fault simulation from the gate-level netlist to the RTL graph. 
% Concurrent fault simulation takes advantage of the locality principle of activity in digital networks\cite{cs} and only simulates activated events in the fault-free network plus any differences that arise due to faults. 
Concurrent fault simulation only simulates activated events in the fault-free network plus any differences that arise due to faults\cite{multi_cs}, which has been used to reduce explicit redundancy. So, we extend the concurrent fault simulation algorithm from gate level to RTL to eliminate the explicit redundancy existing in behavioral nodes. 

