\subsection{Math preliminareis} \label{subsec-math-found}
Suppose $m,n$ be two positive integers and $p$ be a prime number. A Galois field also known as a finite set of elements with two 
%We denote the set of all $n$ binary tuples by $GF(2^{n})=\mathbb{F}_{2}^{n}$ and let $\mathbb{F}_{2}^{n*}=\mathbb{F}_{2}^{n}\setminus \{0\}$.
%The elements of $GF(2^{n})$ can be viewed as vectors in $\mathbb{F}_{2}^{n}$
