	For an S-box $S=(f_{1}, \cdots,f_{m}) \in \mathcal{B}_{n}^{m}$ 
	%and $S=(f_{1},f_{2}, \cdots, f_{m})$
	, the algebraic degree is indicated by $deg_{_{S}}=\max\{deg_{_{f_{j}}} | 1 \leq j \leq m\}$.
	%and  define as the maximum algebraic degree of the component Boolean functions . 
