Then the data stored at server $n,n\in[0:8)$ is given by
\begin{IEEEeqnarray}{c}
\mathcal{Y}_n=\left\{
\begin{array}{@{}ccc@{}}
\tilde{f}_{0}^{(0)}(a_n), & \tilde{f}_{0}^{(1)}(a_n), & \tilde{f}_{0}^{(2)}(a_n) \\
\tilde{f}_{1}^{(0)}(a_n), & \tilde{f}_{1}^{(1)}(a_n), & \tilde{f}_{1}^{(2)}(a_n) \\
\tilde{f}_{2}^{(0)}(a_n), & \tilde{f}_{2}^{(1)}(a_n), & \tilde{f}_{2}^{(2)}(a_n) \\
\end{array}
